[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5529236533","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5529236533","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5529236533,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSZF0NQ","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T17:03:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T17:03:40Z","body":"@bruvzg Is the idea that you can define a common application id in the project settings, but override it in the export options if needed?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5529236533/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5529301463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5529301463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5529301463,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSZJx1w","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T17:09:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T17:09:05Z","body":"> Is the idea that you can define a common application id in the project settings, but override it in the export options if needed?\r\n\r\nYes, but it's not fully common, since ID format is different project settings also have a per-platform list.\r\nThe priority is:\r\n- Use export setting if it is set.\r\n- Use project setting if it is set.\r\n- Generate ID from project name if neither is set.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5529301463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5530122324","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5530122324","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5530122324,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSZ74VA","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T18:14:56Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T18:14:56Z","body":"I'm not sure I understand the intent; application IDs are different enough between platforms than trying to define a project setting one seems a recipe for users confusion and brittle code.\r\n\r\nWhat would be unblocked by having a project setting application ID? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5530122324/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5530177622","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5530177622","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5530177622,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSZ_QVg","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T18:19:35Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T18:19:35Z","body":"> What would be unblocked by having a project setting application ID?\r\n\r\nThis would be helpful for the case where you have, for example, multiple Android export presets and want to use the same application ID for all of them. I frequently forget to copy in the application ID when I add a new Android export preset, and I think this could potentially help with that","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5530177622/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5530247242","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5530247242","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5530247242,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSaDgSg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T18:25:20Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T18:25:20Z","body":"Application IDs are required for desktop notifications on Windows and Linux, it both cases ID is set at runtime and is used when running project from the editor, so it can't be export setting like on Android/iOS/macOS.\nIDs for other platforms, which already have export settings are added for consistency.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5530247242/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5544150455","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5544150455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5544150455,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSnUFtw","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:26:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T17:26:58Z","body":"> > What would be unblocked by having a project setting application ID?\r\n> \r\n> This would be helpful for the case where you have, for example, multiple Android export presets and want to use the same application ID for all of them. I frequently forget to copy in the application ID when I add a new Android export preset, and I think this could potentially help with that\r\n\r\n@dsnopek Sounds like we should also update the export preset duplicate logic to include the application id. Not sure if we can customize what's duplicated per platform though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5544150455/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5544225335","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5544225335","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5544225335,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSnYqNw","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:34:04Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T17:34:22Z","body":"> Application IDs are required for desktop notifications on Windows and Linux, it both cases ID is set at runtime and is used when running project from the editor, so it can't be export setting like on Android/iOS/macOS. IDs for other platforms, which already have export settings are added for consistency.\r\n\r\n@bruvzg Correct me if I'm wrong; today we don't explicitly define application ID for Windows and Linux but instead derive it from `application/config/name`. \r\nWith this PR, we are trying to introduce an explicit application ID, and for platforms that can define application ID at build time, we'll allow the export option to override the application ID defined in the project settings.\r\n\r\nFor platforms that can override the application ID in the export option, how do we guarantee that the value we retrieve at runtime is the correct one?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5544225335/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5544455034","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5544455034","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5544455034,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSnmreg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:55:30Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T17:55:30Z","body":"> Correct me if I'm wrong; today we don't explicitly define application ID for Windows and Linux but instead derive it from application/config/name.\r\n\r\nWe do, but it properly works on Latin names only, can result in non-unique and unreadable IDs.\r\n\r\n> and for platforms that can define application ID at build time, we'll allow the export option to override the application ID defined in the project settings.\r\n\r\nYes, these are existing export settings. I would prefer to remove duplicate export settings, but this would be compatibility breaking.\r\n\r\n> For platforms that can override the application ID in the export option, how do we guarantee that the value we retrieve at runtime is the correct one?\r\n\r\nNone of the platforms with export setting read app ID from project settings at runtime.\r\n\r\nThe only purpose of this change is make it more consistent and allow setting IDs in one place.\r\n\r\nThe situation before this PR is:\r\n- On Android there's export settings, which defaults to generated name (`com.example.$genname`).\r\n- On iOS and macOS, there's export setting with no default value, it must be set manually to export.\r\n- On Windows and Linux it is always generated from the name and can't be overridden.\r\n\r\nWith this change:\r\n- All IDs can be set in the Project Settings. By default, settings are set to `com.example.$genname` (or equivalent string in a platform specific format), so setting ID manually is not required.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5544455034/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5545049331","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5545049331","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5545049331,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSoK88w","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-04T18:46:56Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T18:46:56Z","body":"> Yes, these are existing export settings. I would prefer to remove duplicate export settings, but this would be compatibility breaking.\r\n\r\nOn Android, we still need that capability for more than back-compat reasons. It's common to generate multiple Android export presets, each targeting a different store or Android fork, and use slightly different application IDs (e.g. we use the same approach for the builds of the Android editor targeting the play store / horizon store / pico store).\r\n\r\n> None of the platforms with export setting read app ID from project settings at runtime.\r\n\r\nThat may not be the case now, but if we introduce the application ID project setting, I'd expect features to appear that make use of it, and where users don't realize the difference in the way the application ID is handled between different platforms.\r\n\r\nUsing the example of using different Android application IDs for different Android stores, developers may want to show different messaging / features based on the store their app is downloaded from. To do so, they may end using the application ID project setting without realizing it would not properly reflect the application ID for the exported build.\r\n\r\nI was also discussing with @syntaxerror247 about adding support for notification to Android, similar to what you're doing for Linux and Windows. The Android notifications APIs also do require an application ID, so similar to the previous example, if the application ID project setting is added, we'll need to ensure we use the 'correct' application ID.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5545049331/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5545087378","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122495#issuecomment-5545087378","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122495","id":5545087378,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSoNRkg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-04T18:50:32Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T18:50:32Z","body":"> I was also discussing with @syntaxerror247 about adding support for notification to Android, similar to what you're doing for Linux and Windows. The Android notifications APIs also do require an application ID, so similar to the previous example, if the application ID project setting is added, we'll need to ensure we use the 'correct' application ID.\r\n\r\nIt this case it would make sense to save ID from the exporter in a readable form, I will check it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5545087378/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]